SUMMARY:GO Train Hike - Unionville/Markham
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Bruce Trail Club\nhe villages of Unionville & Markham 
 are connected by the Rouge Valley Trail System following the Rouge River a
 nd running behind the historic buildings on Main Street Unionville\, by Wa
 lden Pond in Austin Drive Park\, through Milne Dam Conservation Area\, and
  ending with a 143 metre long suspension bridge over the dam. We will walk
  into the village of Markham and finish with a short boardwalk trail throu
 gh Tannery Pond which is close to the Markham GO Station. We begin the hik
 e at Unionville GO Station hiking north to the historic Main Street and pi
 cking up the Rouge Valley Trail at Carlton Road. Return to Toronto or the 
 starting point by GO Train or York Region Transit bus. Optional stop at th
 e Rouge River Craft Brewery after the hike.\nTerrain is easy\, mostly pave
 d path/boardwalk with some dirt trails.\nOn The Go Maps Link:\n[https://on
 thegomap.com/s/g5rhpj1s](https://onthegomap.com/s/g5rhpj1s)\n\nBring lunch
 \, water\, snacks\, hat. and insect repellant.\n\nPlease register on the B
 ruce Trail Conservancy website at:\n[https://hikes.brucetrail.org/event/go
 -train-hike-unionville-markham-rouge-river-trail-2/2026-09-13/](https://hi
 kes.brucetrail.org/event/go-train-hike-unionville-markham-rouge-river-trai
 l-2/2026-09-13/)
