SUMMARY:Bus Hike: Limehouse (Bruce Trail Day)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Bruce Trail Club\noin us to celebrate Bruce Trail Day 
 on the trail around Limehouse. For the first 5 km we will hike south from 
 the Sixth Line to Limehouse. The route incorporates the portion of trail r
 emoved from the Fifth Line thanks to those who support the Bruce Trail. We
 'll also pass the seed orchard where native species are grown for the seed
 s to be replanted to re-naturalize other parts of the trail. Those who wan
 t a shorter hike may drop out at Limehouse where information and refreshme
 nts will be available at the Memorial Hall. The second part of the hike wi
 ll be a loop through the Limehouse Conservation area featuring the limesto
 ne kilns\, stone arched bridge\, and a climb through the "hole in the wall
 ". Expect some slightly rocky terrain underfoot and a few moderate hills. 
 Hiking boots or good shoes designed for walking are a must. Those completi
 ng the full 9 km will also have a chance to drop in at the Memorial Hall t
 o learn more about the Bruce Trail and refreshments.\n\nYou must register 
 and prepay the bus fare on the Bruce Trail Conservancy Website (registrati
 on opens Sat Sep 20 8:00 PM (Bus Fares $25 Members/$32 Non-Members (Childr
 en under 12 $10/$14). Bus fares are non-refundable and the hike goes rain 
 or shine.\n\nRegistration Link:\n[https://hikes.brucetrail.org/event/bus-h
 ike-bruce-trail-day-limehouse/2026-10-04/](https://hikes.brucetrail.org/ev
 ent/bus-hike-bruce-trail-day-limehouse/2026-10-04/)
